   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social dialogue on standards-related activities was revitalized thanks to the support of RBSA funding. Results achieved include the approval of Conventions Nos 100 and 138 by the National Parliament, and the submission of reports under ratified Conventions after many years of inactivity. The Office undertook several initiatives within the framework of the RBSA project on strengthening the institutional capacities in Liberia for the ratification, domestication and reporting on ILS, which was implemented in 2020 and 2021. This included, among other activities: (a) an expertized review of the Decent Work Act in a tripartite forum (hybrid workshop), which led to the adoption of a roadmap for the review of the Decent Work Act; (b) a tripartite awareness-raising workshop on Conventions Nos 100 and 138, and (c) a capacity building workshop for constituents on social dialogue to ensure effective engagement of the tripartite partners in the review process. A tripartite reporting workshop on outstanding reports was also undertaken in May 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
