   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Liberia has met its reporting obligations according to Article 22. The government reported on the application of all 13 fundamental, technical and priority conventions it has ratified, and this was done in August 2021. The development of the reports were done in close collaboration with social partners and the other relevant stakeholders with the Ministry of Labour taking the lead.   The social partners, key institutions and agencies with the required information were part of the process. This was made possible due to the capacity-building workshop for Government and Social Partners With funding from the RBSA Project, the ILO engaged two consultants, one international and one national to work with the Government to ensure that all reporting backlogs and that of 2021 are reported. The ILO also facilitated the organization of a validation and capacity-building workshop on article 22 reporting on July 28 and 29, 2021. This workshop brought together all information holders on the various ratified conventions.</narrative>
   </description>
